+   * every ancestor — so a drag that starts on cell text repeatedly clears the
+   * disallow flag mid-gesture and the list steals the drag. Whether the cell or
+   * this view sees the MOVE first is a race, which is why the scroll used to
+   * work only sometimes.
+   *
+   * So: claim tentatively on DOWN (before any cell can interfere), commit the
+   * claim once the drag is horizontal — cancelling the JS touch the same way the
+   * library does for link and checkbox taps — and yield as soon as the drag is
+   * vertical so the chat list still scrolls. `isClaimActive` lets the cells know
+   * not to undo the claim.
